const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文讨论在已有大量因子和重复检验的背景下，应如何提高关于预期收益横截面的统计证据门槛。 阅读时应将其放回原始样本、时点和制度环境中理解，不能把问题本身当作跨市场结论。",en:"The article asks how a large history of proposed factors and repeated tests should change the statistical hurdle for claims about the cross-section of expected returns. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv059",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"研究整理历史因子文献并应用多重检验框架，文献清单、依赖假设与阈值构造都会影响结论。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中任一选择，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It assembles a historical factor-publication inventory and applies a multiple-testing framework, making the inventory, dependence assumptions, and threshold construction material to the result. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv059",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要带日期的论文与因子清单、检验统计量、因子定义、发表时间，以及对依赖性和未公开尝试研究的明确假设。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选必须与原研究分开记录，不能因变量同名或使用最新修订值便视为可比。",en:"Inputs include a dated record of tested factors and papers, test statistics, factor definitions, publication timing, and explicit assumptions about dependence and unobserved research attempts. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv059",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"论文为数据挖掘环境下提高证据门槛提供了理由，并未把某一个t统计量变成普遍接受或否定规则。 它只支持来源描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The paper motivates a higher evidentiary hurdle in a data-mined setting; it does not turn any single t-statistic into a universal acceptance or rejection rule. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv059",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"预先声明因子家族和假设数量；保留发现与验证的时间顺序；记录全部尝试设定；区分探索性证据和确认性证据。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Pre-specify the factor family and hypothesis count; preserve chronological discovery and validation splits; record all tried specifications; and distinguish discovery evidence from confirmatory evidence. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv059",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Review of Financial Studies · DOI record。历史文献盘点与多重检验假设不能认证新信号、解决经济意义问题，或替代样本外与实施审查。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Review of Financial Studies · DOI record. Its historical survey and multiple-testing assumptions do not certify a new signal, resolve economic relevance, or substitute for out-of-sample and implementation review. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhv059",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies · DOI record · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“… and the Cross-Section of Expected Returns”公开说明的研究对象、设计与适用边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。历史文献盘点与多重检验假设不能认证新信号、解决经济意义问题，或替代样本外与实施审查。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “… and the Cross-Section of Expected Returns”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
